{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0aeddd577efa6b777ee8fe7a5ce929cadb80943e8aaba05124e061d84b71abc8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f019c2401ded880c812ae3b6851e6ae05f64e1651ceff5f9758ca7701ea3186"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"An orchestrator LLM delegates to a team of agents via tool calls; two implementations are described: ClaudeCodeOrchestrator (running on Claude Code with agents as MCP tools) and ApiOrchestrator on the Anthropic or Gemini API.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0b89e239530f1af647e39fffff8a078322a46d63f022e131daf82699b93ffb2c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2212f087cd35cdb2048d1d1be512981c8b7c1a2b2d11f80e9515a81b4bb21c08","slc_2f7b647451df3aeb7d2589c585f77b44388f99e3fcf0d522b9e986d0d38d8fdb","slc_42867a0ea9cbb2fc74dba463175294ee1446cebeaefdf72c53f64d6cf99a6bda","slc_661fe417868384222603492216a6a8a05b1f5fec8d358546654f6fd8775b001a","slc_7d718b34bbf3389c8b952de46d6a4a5302ff528a15aa88fc5e7a3658f2a94a50"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Kodo targets Python 3.13+, is installed with uv (uv tool install kodo-agent), and requires at least one agent backend, with Claude Code plus one fast backend (Cursor, Codex, or Gemini CLI) recommended.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0fecf4359da23e32d684e4a579cc57934aef67c3cd9f8f0ceb129133c28ab3e7","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1bf33858ff289a054929beaa43e7d0d71d6fa3b0344171bbdbca4f13103af179"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Four effort levels (low, standard, high, max) scale both orchestrator behavior and verification strictness, from basic test-passing checks up to skeptical rejection of technically correct but mediocre work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_208b61ed0cfb30564a8848adcf0a809b6a51df3395da1f07df1d1157d4abc78b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fa8f6cb5adba19e164d5fae88cc19d5c99ab43369304d2fc482e412f7b2dd17c"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Agents run with full permissions in bypassPermissions mode; they primarily work in the project directory but can access any file on the system, so users are advised to have a git commit or backup before launching.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2c596ed9227d9f5f5c530f96af05829cf110889f277b6360f26c2d60f7777ec9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7330646ab3e8d395ce54716549d282ceadabb60bb51b33b6c9464a5003164a5c","slc_78d2733c380703c5569b45085307d80976fefbe0b888b88e6ed65b77bff16516","slc_a58fa86190c8c8e1303f0ee074fcb67a2610c2c430fa84b0d0fc77fb7af34cd3"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Configuration flags include --team (full default, quick, test), --exchanges, --cycles, --orchestrator (api default, or claude-code/gemini-cli/codex/cursor), --orchestrator-model, --effort, --skip-intake, --auto-refine, --json, and --no-auto-commit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2f529893cb7f1f3f2aee96aedf55c04757de922a1d87e633f63feb1f0d15bfdb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_42a7cbf33f798cf337741acc41c9d5c7c100c6cb0c6c7f245c369a8e6cb18d32","slc_5318e39dad74aa030e2a56b4f4ad637ab2ea5b5c680c771618df687af5a508ee","slc_f66f3f89106afd3fafe43bfe929bbfdf1472557446d3a0af18d95425ea5fb141"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Runs are stored under ~/.kodo/runs/ and can be resumed by ID or as the latest incomplete run; test-mode coverage tracking persists in .kodo/test-coverage.md so repeated runs skip previously tested features.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3b2b5779f156ba13fabcabf542fc58bc8858d72c0a110e9eb05e516447c56dcd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_88806c49169d63630f253773b5c692fe89cb5322995c48b8ff7dda8d766d70ad","slc_a6374f1d63953b8e5a888b0adbb3ea5b6504bde1baaad49e7fc66ef016a2f30b","slc_aba6f9267bdaabcd813497e8d2f51989b932f2a8a6bd51133dfc74fbaade3cba","slc_ec9862ce93029dff2b51cf1703f4eec72f7df3292fd31077d1cfd79778e32484"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Custom teams are defined via team.json with lookup order project-level .kodo/team.json then user-level ~/.kodo/teams/{name}.json; agent fields include backend, model, description, system_prompt, max_turns (default 15), timeout_s, chrome, and fallback_model.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_41f22382a9a0abed077c9c38b70d07c54f6bc7dd173ccd3eea04958a9013a724","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_be67f719b4d8e388713af678e9fed415bd6b39c29b91b8120e3a5d86094882d0"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"An API model is recommended as orchestrator over CLI coding tools because CLI agents tend to write code, micromanage, or go off-script, while a plain API model stays in a coordinator role that delegates.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_464912d44bf7b9c721b93021d9c35ca3414f9ad0617ec5c2507a9af4dc405b0c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4caedcbb68eea1c3d70cf514f70b173aa7fb1a3b0d43df76d1121acbe0eb24a9"],"source_ids":["src_6a111679251f5bdb82ceb252f51ef44b"],"text":"Repository development practice: CLAUDE.md requires autospec=True on all unittest.mock.patch calls (enforced by tests/test_autospec_enforcement.py), spec=RealClass or create_autospec for bare mocks, and a `# noqa: autospec` escape hatch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b9b953b9bd2c7cfa9e70e584fb4a80b7c78136bb943a641d66181de05fb3f49","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f019c2401ded880c812ae3b6851e6ae05f64e1651ceff5f9758ca7701ea3186"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"A session is a stateful conversation with a backend that tracks token usage and supports reset; an agent combines a prompt, session, and turn budget, invoked as agent.run(task, project_dir).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5ef96e5a3b53d406b86cec58595d15fa1ed35fa9663172307e5e075fb1733d63","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4f019c2401ded880c812ae3b6851e6ae05f64e1651ceff5f9758ca7701ea3186"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Work is structured hierarchically: a cycle is one unit of orchestrated work, a run spans multiple cycles with summaries bridging context, and stages are independently verifiable plan pieces that run sequentially or in parallel git worktrees.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_623b7dbe686e15f9dacd4f08353698857d9c55f67d533f1d1a90efd470a9956c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ed4a2e5ea5540fae8bed73a6355d014bfb8b7739b9010e767cfcd7972d46f600"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"The default team comprises an orchestrator plus architect, worker_smart, worker_fast, tester, and tester_browser agents, each with a distinct role such as code survey, implementation, testing, or browser-based UI testing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_69b007aad2bebb7a2f8eba8fe1737089ff6c55df340bd9a60a66e38efe552678","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c1756ca74d2a8519c4be8e5d6e9b98d917b2ad88df1f234ae5501c3da940c45c"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"The API orchestrator expects a GOOGLE_API_KEY (Gemini, described as recommended) or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (Claude alternative) set in .env or the environment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_767ffd831c3bf3500fbbbb734af9e9237b98bddcf7c9dcca446fe9507e042743","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d4db3468dea33dd469f4a90d69f264d54f03df7364216e0943dd67eb7096608"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"A published 100-task head-to-head benchmark using the same underlying model (Cursor composer-1.5) reports that adding Kodo's orchestration layer solves 24% more real-world GitHub issues, with methodology and interactive results available online.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_da0fb545623e3264343a07cf90865aea83a308201e8369d02bc1b919c9d84a8f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d0b6a5b9e1ab9de05357fd1056d814dfc61e479c44494ba39d71da65c1184f6","slc_f5fb72f331fd74d9dd84afea4221ca341752ad3369af1228a7e1aca80cbadece"],"source_ids":["src_671fe625baac55dcb29a2bcddf8366c8"],"text":"Cost tracking separates an API bucket of real pay-per-token spend (e.g. ~$0.13/run for a Gemini Flash orchestrator) from a Virtual bucket showing what subscription-covered worker usage would have cost, which is not actually charged.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_df8a77f656638d0e8c4c86211efa84ff30eeac5391cc6c06472d2fd3587c2cfb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"ikamensh/kodo@51aebbfe5a30 snapshot f4e77a0c0e2eb4e7","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_980aa2954a085edfdf8e2995219910e23de5ede2720eef45aa27aee63d44aff0","slc_9caab8def24c71274323642414341a5e5028ac24d61bf1212d3684231fb11777"],"source_ids":["src_c6ac34e26d685960bfa9fa06b07a726e"],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md documents mocked end-to-end smoke scripts (e.g. scripts/smoke_test_cli.py, run_cli_mocked.py, smoke_test_resume.py) verifying CLI, resume, improve, and interactive flows without API keys, with the full suite run via `uv run pytest tests/` (464 passed, 1 xfailed).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:06:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9d7ce61c6fb8429ebffeb6bd7d6baedc"}
